{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And in the name</b> — \"And in the name I would call, saying 'Please'\" — a language of appeasement with thanks, like אנא נא חטא העם הזה (Exodus 32:32). And I would think in my heart that — [<b>gracious</b> — and merciful is HaShem.]"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 116, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:47.488180648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}